# Project Overview for BulkTrack API

This document provides a guide to the BulkTrack API backend, a Go application running on Cloudflare Workers with D1 as the database.

## 🗺️ High-Level Architecture

The system follows a client-server model where iOS/Web clients communicate via HTTPS (REST) with a Go Edge Worker (Wasm). The worker handles routing, middleware, command/query (CQRS), and domain logic. It interacts with Cloudflare D1 (serverless SQLite) for data storage.

- API Definition: [api/openapi.yaml](mdc:api/openapi.yaml)
- Database Schema: [schema.sql](mdc:schema.sql)

## 🏗️ Layered Design

The codebase is organized into the following layers, with dependencies flowing from Domain to Application to Interface:

- **Domain**: `internal/domain/...` (Entities, VOs, Domain Services - pure Go)
- **Application**: `internal/app/{command,query}` (Use-case orchestration, Tx boundary, DTO ↔ Entity)
- **Interface / Adapter**: `internal/interface/http` (HTTP Router, DTO marshal, Auth/CORS middleware)
- **Infrastructure**: `internal/infrastructure/persistence/d1` (D1 repo impl, KV client, JWT utils)

## 🔌 Middleware Architecture

Middleware is used for CORS, logging, and authentication.
- Global middlewares (CORS, Logging) are applied to most routes.
    - CORS: [internal/interface/http/middleware/cors.go](mdc:internal/interface/http/middleware/cors.go)
    - Logging: [internal/interface/http/middleware/logging.go](mdc:internal/interface/http/middleware/logging.go)
- Route-Specific Middlewares:
    - RequireAuth: [internal/interface/http/middleware/auth.go](mdc:internal/interface/http/middleware/auth.go) (Verifies JWT and injects `uid`)
- Chaining: Implemented in [internal/interface/http/middleware/middleware.go](mdc:internal/interface/http/middleware/middleware.go)
- Router Configuration: Defined in [internal/interface/http/router.go](mdc:internal/interface/http/router.go) and applied in [cmd/worker/main.go](mdc:cmd/worker/main.go).

## 📁 Key Files and Directories

- Entrypoint: [cmd/worker/main.go](mdc:cmd/worker/main.go)
- API Definition: [api/openapi.yaml](mdc:api/openapi.yaml)
- Configuration: [config/config.go](mdc:config/config.go)
- HTTP Router: [internal/interface/http/router.go](mdc:internal/interface/http/router.go)
- Auth Middleware: [internal/interface/http/middleware/auth.go](mdc:internal/interface/http/middleware/auth.go)
- Database Schema: [schema.sql](mdc:schema.sql)
- SQLC Configuration: [internal/infrastructure/persistence/d1/sqlc.yaml](mdc:internal/infrastructure/persistence/d1/sqlc.yaml)
- Cloudflare Workers Config: [wrangler.jsonc](mdc:wrangler.jsonc)

## 📦 Data Modeling

The primary database schema is defined in [schema.sql](mdc:schema.sql). Default partitioning is by `device_id`.

## 🛠️ Build & Local Development

- SQLC queries are generated based on [internal/infrastructure/persistence/d1/sqlc.yaml](mdc:internal/infrastructure/persistence/d1/sqlc.yaml).
- Cloudflare Wrangler is used for deployment and local development (`wrangler dev`, `wrangler d1`).

## 🪵 Logging Strategy

- Uses standard Go `log` package.
- Basic HTTP request/response logging is handled by middleware: [internal/interface/http/middleware/logging.go](mdc:internal/interface/http/middleware/logging.go).
